latest_plan = "Based on the reflection, here's a step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Analyze the input grid:\n   - Determine grid dimensions\n   - Identify unique colors present\n\n2. Create a color transformation map:\n   - If orange (7) is present: map blue (1) <-> orange (7)\n   - If orange (7) is not present: map blue (1) <-> sky (8)\n   - Always map red (2) <-> green (3)\n   - Other colors remain unchanged\n\n3. Perform vertical flip and color transformation:\n   - Create a new grid with rows in reverse order\n   - Apply the color transformation to each cell\n\n4. Identify and transform patterns:\n   - For each non-black color:\n     a. Find connected regions\n     b. For each region:\n        - Calculate its current position and dimensions\n        - Determine the new position (opposite corner)\n        - Attempt to expand the pattern if space allows\n        - If expansion is not possible, try to maintain original size\n        - If original size doesn't fit, contract the pattern\n        - Move the transformed pattern to the new position\n\n5. Adjust patterns to fit available space:\n   - If a pattern can be expanded vertically or horizontally, do so\n   - If a pattern needs to be contracted, remove cells from the edges while maintaining the overall shape\n\n6. Fine-tune pattern positions:\n   - Ensure patterns don't overlap\n   - Adjust positions slightly if needed to better utilize space\n\n7. Return the transformed grid\n\nImplementation details:\n\n- Use the ColoredGrid class methods for grid operations\n- Implement helper functions for each major step:\n  - create_color_map(unique_colors)\n  - vertical_flip_and_transform(grid, color_map)\n  - transform_pattern(grid, region)\n  - expand_pattern(grid, region, new_position)\n  - contract_pattern(grid, region, new_position)\n  - move_pattern(grid, region, new_position)\n\n- Use depth-first search or breadth-first search for finding connected regions\n- Implement pattern transformation logic that preserves the general shape and concept of each pattern while adapting to the new grid configuration\n\nThis plan addresses all the key aspects of the transformation: vertical flipping, color swapping, pattern relocation, and pattern adjustment. It also allows for flexibility in handling different input grids and pattern shapes."
